<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Samancor half year shr slumps, div halved.</title>
<headline>Samancor half year shr slumps, div halved.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     90	    vs 201</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 30	    vs 60</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   171.43	vs 381.92</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   263.35	vs 496.78</p>
<p>    Tax			 81.59	 vs 135.61</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   7.11	  vs 0.22</p>
<p>    Attrib to outside     23.67	 vs 10.34</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,754.73    vs 1,860.55</p>
<p>Div payable March 27</p>
<p>on register March7</p>
<p>Full name: Samancor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings per share of between 90 to 110 cents and a dividend on a range of 42 to 60 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
